WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(audience clapping)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.400
- Do either one of you know Nick Offerman?

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.820
- [Celebrity] Not personally.

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.910
- I have known Nick
Offerman for a long time.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:08.820
Megan Mullally is one of
my dear friends, his wife.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.653
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:00:09.653 --> 00:00:13.290
- We did the revival of
Greece together back in 1994.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.760
- I love it.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:15.917
- You know, so I've, I've
known them for a great...

00:00:15.917 --> 00:00:18.900
- Such a great couple and I
love that he's so talented.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.000
He's a man of many, many talents, y'all.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.570
He's an actor, a comedian, an
author, and in the vein of one

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:26.820
of these things is not like the other.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.350
He's a woodworker too.

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.570
He literally can build you like a canoe.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:31.830
Like it's crazy.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.290
Last week when we were in
rehearsals getting ready to

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:36.750
launch this new season, I was
surprised when Nick popped

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.570
up here on the stage looking
very dashing by the way.

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:41.310
And apparently he just wanted to make sure

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.920
that the studio was in tiptop
shape for our new season here

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:45.450
in New York, and he wanted
make sure it's safe,

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:46.592
so check this out.

00:00:46.592 --> 00:00:47.890
(audience clapping)

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.979
(crew members chatting)

00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:51.790
(guitar strumming)

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:52.765
- [Director] Practice the walk over here.

00:00:52.765 --> 00:00:54.079
This is your first guest.

00:00:54.079 --> 00:00:55.830
You'll come out, we just
gotta stand them coming in.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:56.870
- Okay.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.590
- All right everybody, standby.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:00:59.423
- Woo.

00:00:59.423 --> 00:01:00.330
- Here we go.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.163
- Alright everybody.

00:01:01.163 --> 00:01:03.270
Our first guest is the only person ever,

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.210
woman or man, to win the three big awards

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.100
for film, TV, and stage acting
in both the US and the UK.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.413
Please give it up for dame Helen Mirren.

00:01:14.491 --> 00:01:17.732
(upbeat show music)

00:01:17.732 --> 00:01:19.470
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.572
- [Kelly] You look so handsome.

00:01:21.572 --> 00:01:23.045
- Kelly, you look so beautiful.

00:01:23.045 --> 00:01:24.090
- What are you doing here?

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.740
- I was just in the neighborhood.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.830
Moving into a new home
is always difficult,

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.150
and I happened to be in the neighborhood

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:33.420
so I thought I'd stop by and offer Kelly

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.760
any I help that I possibly could.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.003
- Do you like what we're
we've got going on?

00:01:37.003 --> 00:01:37.836
- I do.

00:01:37.836 --> 00:01:39.550
I see some walnut. I see some oak.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:41.280
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.113
Sturdy.

00:01:42.113 --> 00:01:42.960
- Yeah.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.400
- We gotta bought a box of games.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.634
- Oh, it's my podium.

00:01:45.634 --> 00:01:46.467
- I know.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.150
We've still got the lectern of integrity.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.370
- [Nick] And as I was looking
around the set, I noticed,

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:52.530
you know, gratifyingly,
that they had brought

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.230
my lectern of integrity with them.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.000
Can you tell me why does it say Jonas?

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:57.900
- [Kelly] Well, here's the thing,

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.130
Nick Jonas came and, you know,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.130
we wanted to make him just feel special.

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.383
Still yours.

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:04.290
- Is he still a furniture builder?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.491
- No, I don't think so.

00:02:06.491 --> 00:02:07.324
- Oh.

00:02:07.324 --> 00:02:08.370
- Huh.

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:13.370
- A musician named Nick
Jonas had added his name.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.663
Might as well have been Judas.

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:18.863
There we go.

00:02:18.863 --> 00:02:19.696
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:19.696 --> 00:02:21.090
- [Nick] I've got some
sandpaper right here.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.105
We call that an East Coast touch up.

00:02:23.105 --> 00:02:23.938
- I like it.

00:02:23.938 --> 00:02:25.560
- [Nick] I mean, you know,
the, the scuttlebutt is

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.833
that Joe Jonas is very nice,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.210
but apparently Nick is
a real piece of (beep).

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.820
Well, I guess since we're here and...

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:36.750
- What's this?

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.520
- I'm actually in town promoting

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.550
the paperback release of my last book.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.570
- Thank you.

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:44.047
- [Nick] To merth, heart,

00:02:46.838 --> 00:02:48.338
Jonas can suck it.

00:02:50.351 --> 00:02:52.086
- [Kelly] Suck it. (laughs)

00:02:52.086 --> 00:02:53.803
(crew laughing)

00:02:53.803 --> 00:02:54.636
I love it.

00:02:54.636 --> 00:02:55.710
- That'll show him.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.543
- I know.

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.330
- It's relatively well known that

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.340
I know my way around a toolbox.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.650
So thought I'd sneak in and see

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:09.300
if they could use any help
with my expertise in scenery.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.800
- [Director] So standby,

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.872
and just do a little reading here.

00:03:12.872 --> 00:03:13.838
- Okay. Perfect.

00:03:13.838 --> 00:03:14.730
- [Director] See how it's going, okay?

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:15.563
- Alright everybody

00:03:15.563 --> 00:03:17.970
so our first guest is the only person ever

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.640
woman or man to win the
three big awards for

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.411
film, TV, and stage acting
in both the US and the UK.

00:03:25.411 --> 00:03:27.810
(tape measure rattling)

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:28.643
What's going on?

00:03:28.643 --> 00:03:29.910
Is it pretty good or?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.770
- [Nick] I've been known
to be handy with a hammer

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.520
or a tape measure or roll of drywall tape.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.520
Is that just for rehearsal or
is this table gonna stay here?

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.520
- You know, I think it might be staying.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.230
- Alright. You might want to

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.030
you might wanna replenish the finish.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.193
- Oh.

00:03:46.193 --> 00:03:48.600
- [Nick] And it looks
cool, but you don't wanna

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.770
spill gravy in it.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.830
- Okay, well I don't wanna spill
gravy, I just wanna eat it.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:53.790
I don't wanna spill any of it.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.140
- There's one place to
spill gravy, am I right?

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.203
In the gravy hole.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.170
- Alright everybody, we
always like to close out

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:04.353
with something trending online,
so this is what I'm liking.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:08.340
Hey, what's up Nick?

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.110
- Oh hey, sorry.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:10.943
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:10.943 --> 00:04:11.776
- Don't worry about me.

00:04:11.776 --> 00:04:15.030
We're just finishing up some final tweaks.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.460
Do you know who did this tuck pointing?

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:18.450
- I, you know what?

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.360
I don't even know what you
said if I'm being honest.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.770
- All right.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.450
- Okay. Alright, well you keep doing you.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.410
- [Nick] Alright.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.243
- Thank you.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.400
- The risers at first glance
are solid, but the pine

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.010
that they used for the structure
is a little bit naughty

00:04:35.010 --> 00:04:37.620
and eventually that's
gonna need reinforcement,

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:39.843
but for now, it should be fine.

00:04:41.730 --> 00:04:44.340
The coffin locks that
they're using to lock

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.990
in the platforms seem to
be like an aluminum alloy.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.080
Yes, they're a little bit
cheaper, but come check with me

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.770
in three years and see if those
things are still operating.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:59.970
The conniption rods won't
last you more than 18 months.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.403
Hope I was able to help out a little bit.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.550
I'm glad to be a good
neighbor whenever I can.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.160
And best of luck to Kelly
with the new season.

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:10.020
I'm sure it's gonna be terrific.

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:11.223
Can't wait to come back.

00:05:13.699 --> 00:05:16.866
(door handle rattles)

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:20.543
Piece of (beep).

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:25.273
(door unlocking)

00:05:25.273 --> 00:05:26.106
I got it.

00:05:29.372 --> 00:05:31.572
(audience cheering)

00:05:31.572 --> 00:05:32.856
- One more time, y'all.

00:05:32.856 --> 00:05:35.289
Give it up Nick Offerman.

00:05:35.289 --> 00:05:36.247
- Woo.

00:05:36.247 --> 00:05:37.515
- [Kelly] Love him so much.

00:05:37.515 --> 00:05:40.499
His book, Where the Deer and Antelope Play

00:05:40.499 --> 00:05:43.128
is now available in paperback,
and it will be on permanent

00:05:43.128 --> 00:05:46.211
display on my set because I love him.

00:05:48.103 --> 00:05:49.350
Alright, so you can also see Nick

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:51.420
on his US comedy tour right now.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:52.560
He's hilarious. Go see him.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:53.820
You'll feel good about yourself.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:56.163
Go online for tickets
if you wanna go see it.

